The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (uvc_parse_control(dev) < 0) {
    uvc_trace(UVC_TRACE_PROBE, "Unable to parse UVC descriptors.\n");
    goto error;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if the parsing of the UVC control descriptors fails, the code jumps to the error handling path without ensuring that the media device has been initialized. This can lead to dereferencing uninitialized pointers, which may cause a crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
/* Initialize the media device. */
#ifdef CONFIG_MEDIA_CONTROLLER
dev->mdev.dev = &intf->dev;
strscpy(dev->mdev.model, dev->name, sizeof(dev->mdev.model));
if (udev->serial)
    strscpy(dev->mdev.serial, udev->serial, sizeof(dev->mdev.serial));
usb_make_path(udev, dev->mdev.bus_info, sizeof(dev->mdev.bus_info));
dev->mdev.hw_revision = le16_to_cpu(udev->descriptor.bcdDevice);
media_device_init(&dev->mdev);
dev->vdev.mdev = &dev->mdev;
#endif
```
Reason:
The fix initializes the media device before the error handling path can be reached. This ensures that the media device is properly set up, preventing dereferencing of uninitialized pointers during cleanup in the error path, thus avoiding potential crashes.

